            <ArticleTitle>Single coronary artery from right aortic sinus giving rise to left main coronary artery and a hypoplastic right coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E112-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery anomalies are uncommon and the occurrence of a single coronary artery with no structural heart disease is very rare. We report a hitherto undescribed type of single coronary artery originating from the right aortic sinus giving rise to left main coronary artery and right coronary artery that was hypoplastic proximally.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
